.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-GET-OBJECT-SIZE 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-get-object-size \- an object's size in bytes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm get-object-size
.RB ( \-\-bucket | \-b
.I NAME|ERN
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I KEY
|
.BR \-\-ern | \-e
.IR ERN )
.RB [ \-\-bytes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Returns an object's size in bytes, without downloading it: the object's ERN,
bucket, key and
.BR size .
.PP
An object whose upload has not finished has no final size yet and is refused
with its status, as
.B get-object
refuses it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fINAME|ERN\fR
The object's bucket, by name or ERN. With
.BR \-\-key .
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
The object's key within the bucket.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
The object's ERN, instead of
.B \-\-bucket
and
.BR \-\-key .
.TP
.B \-\-bytes
Print only the size, as a number, for a script.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli esm get-object-size -b incoming -k deliveries/onix.xml
size=$(euclid-cli esm get-object-size -b incoming -k deliveries/onix.xml --bytes)
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The size was printed.
.TP
.B 1
No such object, an upload not yet finished, not permitted, or invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket-size (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
